I've finished the game and after some time reflecting this is my review:
Pros:
- Amazing, mature and brutal story;
- Decisions have different outcomes;
- Great and memorable characters;
- Npc's do different activities throughout the day/night;
- Very atmospheric ( citys, inn)
- Different tallents to choose;
Cons:
- Combat was pretty bad, sometimes even frustrating ( enemies scaling difficulty);
- There's some invisible walls ( normal for older games though);
- Npc's and enemies can block your way;
Final Verdic: 7,5 / 10
In my opinion this game could reach an 8,5 or even a 9 if not for the combat, but I can easily recomend this one for any RPG lover or Witcher 3 fans out there to come play this one.

